    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite is green (34 tests, 0 failures).\n\nHere's what I did:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Replaced the `membershipTier` (string) response field with `membershipLevel` (integer, 1\u20133), so the generated `OwnerDto` now exposes `membershipLevel` instead of `membershipTier`.\n\n2. **`Memberships.java`** (new util) \u2014 Added `membershipLevel(email, namesakeCount)`: starts at 1, `+1` if an email is present, `+1` if `namesakeCount == 0`, capped at 3. Documented that level 4 is reserved for tenure.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Swapped the old `membershipTier` MapStruct expression (with the GOLD/SILVER/BRONZE logic) for one that maps `membershipLevel` via the new helper.\n\n4. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 Mapped the DTO before emitting the create audit line and added `membershipLevel={}` to it (records the level instead of a tier), and updated the two doc comments that referenced the audit fields and the now-removed GOLD tier.\n\nNote: the `householdSize` field (which fed the old GOLD tier) is still computed and stored, but it no longer influences membership \u2014 consistent with the spec, which derives the level solely from email and namesakeCount.",
